+# Approved voices reused by jobs (v7.0.85)
+
+## What was happening
+
+After Create step 4 approves the narration and "Prepare all selected TTS" has built the voices, a job still ran
+the script localization and the TTS again for every language. The job log showed:
+
+- `Voice ready via reviewed-prepared-narration` (the master voice from the approved batch was used), then
+- `Localizing the approved master script HI` and `OR` (Gemini Web drafts), then
+- `Preparing TTS and word timings EN`, `HI` and `OR` (new TTS calls).
+
+Every language's voice was spent twice.
+
+## Cause
+
+When a job attached the approved batch, it reused the voices only if every card and hook setting matched the batch
+exactly (text cards, educational, hooks). One difference, for example a text-card or hook checkbox changed after the
+batch was prepared, caused the job to build everything again: scripts, then TTS for every language. The narration
+text itself was not the cause; the voice check had already passed.
+
+## What changed
+
+- A job reuses the approved voices whenever the audio files and the master narration still match. The text-card,
+  educational and hook settings no longer decide whether TTS is repeated.
+- When those settings differ, only the cards are drafted again (Gemini Web text, not TTS), and only for the languages
+  affected. Hooks are drafted only when they are newly requested.
+- If no matching voices exist, the job builds them once, from the approved snapshot.
+- The job log says when no approved narration was found for the master, so a repeat can be explained. The line reads:
+  `No approved narration found for this master and languages; drafting it for review (no TTS yet)`.
+
+## Still to confirm
+
+- The cause of a repeated localization on a job whose batch was approved has not been reproduced here. If the job log
+  still shows the "No approved narration found" line after this update, send `production/language_editions.json` and
+  the `speech_preparation/scripts/` folder names from the Create step 4 batch.
+- Gemini Web card drafts are still sent again when a card or hook setting changes. These use the Gemini Web
+  daily limit, not the TTS limit.
+
+## Files
+
+- `engine/speech_cards.py`: `prepare_selected_editions` (voice reuse), `prepare_batch` (log line when no approved
+  narration is found).
+- `tests/test_v785_voice_reuse.py` (new, 4 tests).
+- `tools/update_v784_to_v785.py`: updater from 7.0.84.
